    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Strong momentum continues in the payer business, with accelerating session volumes and expanding covered lives driving utilization. The company now reaches over 200 million covered lives, reflecting deepening integration with existing clients and new partnerships. Demand for telehealth mental services appears robust, and the firm is actively leveraging AI technology to enhance operations and service delivery. There are no indications of softening macro pressures or competitive displacement in the reported period.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership has executed on multiple fronts: profitability improvements, a share repurchase program, and a bolt-on acquisition (Wizzo) that modestly adds to future growth. Marketing efficiency gains were highlighted, with reduced spend alongside rising brand recognition. Despite these operational wins, the market narrative has turned more cautious; following a run-up to a 52-week high, several analysts downgraded the stock to Hold, suggesting the positive execution is now largely reflected in expectations.",
